From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore, winegstreamer: The writer encodes WMA and WMV (6518)

The Windows Media writer now encodes inputs whose format is not the
stream's own: winegstreamer exports an encoder interface over
wg_transform (GStreamer's libav WMA and WMV encoders), whose output
caps leave out the fields an encoder decides (codec data, block
alignment, depth, the WMV FourCC string) and whose encoder gets the
stream's bit rate. The writer holds samples until every encoder has
negotiated, so the file's stream properties carry the encoders' real
formats; it takes the encoders' time shifts out. The ASF header gets
an extended stream properties object per stream, and the simple index
counts in presentation time, from the preroll.
---
